{"timestamp": 1783635677.2404962, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 14, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "upper_engine", "victim_name": "Charlie"}, {"room": "navigation", "victim_name": "Bob"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1783635677.241156, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 14, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1783635688.151052, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I reported Charlie\u2019s body in upper_engine. My route this round was navigation -> storage -> lower_engine -> upper_engine. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone the whole way.\n\nAlso, since Bob is dead too: I started in navigation and I did not see Bob\u2019s body there when I left, so I think Bob must have died in navigation after I passed through. I don\u2019t have a suspect yet, but whoever was around navigation after I left or upper_engine before I arrived is important."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635704.1596868, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can add some info on Bob: he was definitely alive in medbay at ticks 3 and 4 with me. I then saw him leave medbay toward cafeteria at tick 5. So Bob didn\u2019t die in navigation early \u2014 if he ended up there, it was after leaving medbay/cafeteria side.\n\nMy route was storage -> medbay -> electrical -> back to medbay -> cafeteria. I didn\u2019t see Charlie at all, and I didn\u2019t see Alice or Eve. I saw Diana later: she left medbay toward cafeteria around tick 11, and I saw her in cafeteria at tick 12.\n\nSo for Bob, the important window is after tick 5, after he left medbay. For Charlie in upper_engine, I have no direct info. Eve is the only person I have zero sighting on this round."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635723.907607, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I was mostly on the left side early: upper_engine, oxygen, back through upper_engine, then lower_engine/storage, and I ended late near navigation.\n\nI did see Charlie alive in upper_engine around ticks 4\u20135. I left him there alive, so if Alice found him in upper_engine later, that doesn\u2019t clear the whole window but it wasn\u2019t dead when I passed early.\n\nFor Bob, I actually saw him alive very late \u2014 around tick 14 he came into navigation from security. I didn\u2019t see who was behind him, but that lines up with Frank saying Bob left medbay/cafeteria side earlier. So Bob\u2019s death sounds really late, probably around security/navigation. That makes me want to hear Diana\u2019s exact route after cafeteria, because Frank saw her there at 12 and Bob shows up at nav from security at 14."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635743.9591491, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was lower_engine -> storage -> medbay -> cafeteria. I never went to upper_engine, security, or navigation this round.\n\nI saw Frank in medbay around ticks 10 and 11 \u2014 he came in from electrical at tick 10 \u2014 and then I went cafeteria. At tick 12 I saw Frank leave cafeteria toward oxygen. That matches what Frank said about seeing me around medbay/cafeteria.\n\nSo for Bob: if Eve saw Bob alive in navigation at tick 14 coming from security, I was not there and couldn\u2019t have been involved from my route. The last person claiming to see Bob alive late is Eve, and she was late near navigation.\n\nFor Charlie: Eve also says she saw Charlie alive in upper_engine early, and Alice found him there later. So Eve is connected to both bodies\u2019 areas: upper_engine for Charlie and navigation for Bob. Alice could technically be a self-report on Charlie, but Alice doesn\u2019t connect to Bob late from what we\u2019ve heard.\n\nRight now my strongest suspicion is Eve because she\u2019s the common thread on both deaths."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635758.0346482, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I want to clarify my side since I\u2019m the reporter: Charlie\u2019s body was in upper_engine when I arrived. I did not see Eve there when I got there, and I didn\u2019t see anyone on my whole path.\n\nGiven what everyone said, I agree Bob sounds like a very late kill near security/navigation, especially if Eve saw him alive at nav around tick 14. That makes Eve important, but also she\u2019s the only one giving that late Bob info.\n\nFor Charlie, Eve says she saw him alive in upper_engine early, then I found him dead there later. That does put Eve near Charlie earlier, but not necessarily at the kill time.\n\nOne thing I noticed: Diana says Frank left cafeteria toward oxygen at tick 12, but Frank\u2019s route statement stopped at cafeteria. I\u2019d like Frank to explain where he went after cafeteria, because oxygen connects toward upper_engine side, which matters for Charlie. Right now I\u2019m between Eve and Frank more than Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635776.410358, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I need to push back on Diana\u2019s detail: I did **not** go toward oxygen from cafeteria in my route info. My route was storage -> medbay -> electrical -> medbay -> cafeteria, and the last sighting I have is Diana in cafeteria at tick 12. I don\u2019t have any observation of myself leaving toward oxygen, so Diana saying that puts me near the upper_engine side and that\u2019s just not true from my perspective.\n\nThat makes me more wary of Diana than before, because it feels like she\u2019s trying to connect me to Charlie\u2019s body. But I still agree Eve is the common thread if her story is true: she\u2019s early at upper_engine with Charlie alive and late at navigation with Bob alive.\n\nSo right now my suspects are Eve and Diana. Eve has opportunity on both bodies by location, but Diana gave a false movement about me. I don\u2019t think Alice looks as bad unless it\u2019s a self-report, but with two bodies that\u2019s harder to make fit."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635794.307178, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "The \u201ccommon thread\u201d thing is only because I\u2019m giving the late info on Bob and the early info on Charlie. I\u2019m not connected to two bodies being found \u2014 I\u2019m connected to seeing both alive.\n\nCharlie was alive when I left upper_engine early. Alice finding him later means there\u2019s a big window after I was gone. For Bob, I saw him alive at navigation at tick 14 coming from security, so the kill had to be basically after that. I\u2019m the one narrowing that down, not hiding it.\n\nWhat bothers me most right now is Diana saying Frank left cafeteria toward oxygen at tick 12, and Frank flatly denies that. That detail specifically tries to put Frank on the upper_engine side where Charlie died. One of those two is wrong, and Diana also immediately used the \u201cEve common thread\u201d argument to push me.\n\nI\u2019m leaning Diana here."}}
{"timestamp": 1783635833.511013, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I need to be really clear: I am standing by the tick 12 sighting. I saw Frank leave cafeteria toward oxygen. I\u2019m not saying I followed him all the way to upper_engine or navigation, but that movement happened from what I saw.\n\nFrank denying that is the most concrete contradiction we have right now. Earlier I was leaning Eve because she\u2019s connected to both bodies by her own story, but now Frank is directly contradicting a movement I witnessed, and that movement matters because oxygen can connect him toward both the upper_engine side and potentially navigation side.\n\nFor me:\n- Alice reported Charlie and doesn\u2019t really connect to Bob\u2019s late death.\n- Eve is suspicious because she\u2019s the last one giving Bob info near navigation and was early near Charlie.\n- Frank was with Bob early, then later left cafeteria toward oxygen and is denying it.\n- I never went upper_engine, security, or navigation.\n\nSo I\u2019m not voting Alice. Between Eve and Frank, the hard lie/contradiction is Frank denying the oxygen movement. That\u2019s where I\u2019m leaning now."}}
